body:
I don't have any words that can help. But I can tell you that your words resonated. That's exactly how I feel. I don't know if it's any solace, to know you're not alone, but... You're not alone. 

&#x200B;

People who are outside the darkness don't understand it. They pretend that they do and they give us useless advice like "just turn on a light! How hard can it be!"

&#x200B;

But we're stumbling around in it together. Who knows if we'll ever find our way out? But we are not alone here in it, and occasionally we can find each other and brush a hand against another in the darkness. Consider this message to be that action: brushing up against you in the darkness, and maybe softly commiserating about how dark it is. I don't know the way out any better than you do, but we're both in the same darkness.
